  "privacyFilesAndBackupsTitle": "Files and backups",
  "privacyFilesAndBackupsBody": "Configuration and plugin contents, source addresses, and credentials saved in them are stored in the app's private directory without additional application-level encryption. Exported ZIP files are not encrypted and include configurations, plugins, app settings, and the source addresses and credentials saved in them. Backup import and export are available under Settings → Storage and data and use Android's file picker; you choose where exported files are saved.\n\nAndroid system backup and device transfer can copy configurations, plugins, and app settings. Whether they are enabled depends on system settings and the backup service in use. A file provider's synchronization features can also keep cloud copies of selected files.",
  "privacyRecordsAndLogsTitle": "Connection records, core logs, and original content",
  "privacyRecordsAndLogsBody": "Recent connection records and logs are held only in device memory, within bounded capacities and retention windows. They are not saved as history files. You can clear them on their respective pages; they disappear when the process ends.\n\nSettings → Diagnostics → Core logs displays core operation, connection, and error messages. Retained logs show original core messages. When capacity is insufficient, whole entries are removed or skipped and omissions are reported; message content is not truncated or rewritten. The configuration editor and backups retain original content.",
